{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6c8b48289b550bf61cce907438d4dcefa003982c7ff040728cdf6a33a5dee491","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira adapter value map consolidation","key_entities":["_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE","adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py","adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py","LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA","test_exactly_one_type_map_literal_within_adapters","test_outbound_differ_session_log_exclusion.py"],"problem_keywords":["code duplication","value map","single source of truth","guard","jira integration"],"propositions":["The ticket-type map (_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE) is duplicated in two locations: Cloud adapter and DC backend, creating risk of silent divergence between deployments.","The existing guard for status and priority maps does not extend to the ticket-type map, leaving it unprotected against future duplication.","Both copies are content-identical (four keys mapping task/story/bug/epic to Task/Story/Bug/Epic with identical values, differing only in key order).","The solution consolidates the map into adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py and imports it under the historical alias in both create paths, following the J2 precedent pattern.","The guard must be extended to cover ticket-type maps and mutation-checked by reintroducing a second literal and verifying the test fails."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787638132156202507,"uuid":"9dc7e9f4-3bb3-400b-8981-1142f1b449e5"}